: so outcomes are: from A: -4000, -2000, 0; from B: -6000, 0. So all outcomes: -4000, -2000, 0, -6000, 0. That's five values. The average is (-4000 -2000 + 0 -6000 + 0)/5 = (-12000)/5 = -2400. Now, for each lottery, count how many of its outcomes are higher than -2400. Lottery A: outcomes -4000 (≤ -2400), -2000 (> -2400), 0 (> -2400) → two outcomes higher. Lottery B: -6000 (≤ -2400), 0 (> -2400) → one outcome higher. So the reason prefers Lottery A, which has more outcomes above the average of -2400. Thus, the reason can be applied and prefers A.",
